      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This seems to be directly caused by another issue: avatars not updated for Unity 2017 will ignore a camera's near clip plane. If a model is closer than the near clip plane, it will be properly clipped if reuploaded for Unity 2017, but models uploaded in 5.6 will still render.\n\nIn this screenshot, I have a camera on my hand. I am updated, the person next to me is not: https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/465599985036165124/522414927756132370/20181212011223_1.jpg",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
